      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "File verification is a common experience in today's world (think steam launcher, Oculus store, etc.) They check the file checksum and edit date against that of the server and if nothing changed, use the local copy.\n\nIt absolutely blows my mind this hasn't been added to VRChat yet because yes, it's always a good idea to optimize worlds to begin with, sometimes even the most well optimized and properly designed worlds are still 100+ MB \n\nPlease fix this! This should be one of the first things done back when the world systems update was done",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-21T00:30:57.486Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Could file verification of unchanged files (textures, etc.) be added to reduce the time required to redownload/update worlds. After you've loaded a world it shouldn't have to redownload EVERYTHING again, it's a big waste of time. I dread changing to 100+MB worlds some worlds take forever to redownload everything. I have 2MB/s download and vrchat servers only output 0.25MB/s average to Australia :/ .",
